---
import SealedSection from '../seal/SealedSection.astro';
import ShotCarousel from '../ui/ShotCarousel.tsx';

import planMode from '../../assets/concepts/plan-mode-surface.svg?raw';
import cdConfine from '../../assets/concepts/cd-confinement.svg?raw';
import permMerge from '../../assets/concepts/permission-merge.svg?raw';
import guardSwitch from '../../assets/concepts/guardrails-switch.svg?raw';
import fanOut from '../../assets/concepts/fan-out.svg?raw';
import credRes from '../../assets/concepts/credential-resolution.svg?raw';
import processSupervision from '../../assets/concepts/process-supervision.svg?raw';

import planReviewShot from '../../assets/shots/plan-review.svg';
import approvalDiffShot from '../../assets/shots/approval-diff.svg';
import permissionsShot from '../../assets/shots/permissions.svg';
import agentsRosterShot from '../../assets/shots/agents-roster.svg';
import footerShot from '../../assets/shots/footer.svg';
import modelPickerShot from '../../assets/shots/model-picker.svg';
import localModelShot from '../../assets/shots/local-model.svg';
---

<SealedSection label="modes" sealText="Modes: agent for general coding, plan for read-only investigation with Bash absent, and goal for one tracked objective. Explicit choices are sticky and never re-classified." id="modes">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
    <div class="order-2 lg:order-1 space-y-4">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink p-2" aria-hidden="true"><Fragment set:html={planMode} /></div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-measure order-1 lg:order-2">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-vx-ink">Modes.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        Three modes, one fail-closed surface. Signet classifies a mode-less prompt into agent, plan,
        or goal, and an explicit choice is never re-guessed.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        <strong>Agent</strong> is the default for general coding. The full tool surface sits behind the
        permission gates, and the security classifier runs on every untrusted result.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        <strong>Plan</strong> reads before it changes. The surface is fail-closed with <code class="mono">Bash</code> absent,
        not present-but-gated: a model cannot call what is not advertised. A read-only{' '}
        <code class="mono">Bash</code> returns only under an explicit allow rule, and the plan is a structured,
        persisted document you approve.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        <strong>Goal</strong> pursues one named objective to completion. A todo list built only from assistant
        text tracks the work, and the loop keeps going while the objective advances.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        Not sure what it would pick? <code class="mono">-detect-mode</code> prints the decision without acting on it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 max-w-[72ch]">
    <ShotCarousel
      client:load
      shots={[{ src: planReviewShot.src, alt: 'The plan review pane with Approve, Refine and Cancel', caption: 'plan review pane' }]}
    />
  </div>
</SealedSection>

<SealedSection label="tools" sealText="Tools first class: a fixed-argv native catalogue of read-only utilities, never a shell. Cd is confined so the working directory moves inside the session root and the root does not widen." id="tools">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
    <div class="prose-measure">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-vx-ink">Tools.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        A fixed-argv native catalogue of read-only utilities: <code class="mono">Cat</code>, <code class="mono">Head</code>,{' '}
        <code class="mono">Git</code>, <code class="mono">JQ</code>, <code class="mono">Find</code>, <code class="mono">Diff</code>, and about 19 more. Each is
        backed by a specific binary and a fixed argument shape passed straight to{' '}
        <code class="mono">exec.Command</code>, never through a shell. Arbitrary command strings are rejected.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        <code class="mono">Cd</code> is confined: the working directory moves <em>inside</em> the session root, and the
        root does not widen. Path traversal to <code class="mono">../../../etc</code> is blocked, not warned about.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink p-2" aria-hidden="true"><Fragment set:html={cdConfine} /></div>
  </div>
</SealedSection>

<SealedSection label="diagnostics" sealText="Diagnostics: the harness checks the file the model just edited and hands the errors back on the same tool result. Language servers detected on PATH, fixed-argv syntax checks when none is installed, per-language on/off in /settings. Every message is capped, flattened to one line, stripped of control runes, and sealed with a nonce and a SHA-256." id="diagnostics">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
    <div class="prose-measure">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-vx-ink">Diagnostics.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        The harness checks the file the model just edited and hands the errors back on the same{' '}
        <code class="mono">Edit</code> result. No extra round trip, no <code class="mono">Bash</code> build in between.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        Language servers are detected on <code class="mono">PATH</code>. When none is installed, fixed-argv syntax
        checks like <code class="mono">gofmt -e</code>, <code class="mono">bash -n</code>, <code class="mono">ruby -c</code> and{' '}
        <code class="mono">zig ast-check</code> take over. Each language can be toggled in <code class="mono">/settings</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink/30 p-4">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-vx-ink">Same turn</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-vx-ink/80">Errors ride back on the tool result itself.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink/30 p-4">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-vx-ink">Fourteen languages</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-vx-ink/80">Go, TypeScript, Python, Rust, C, C++, Obj-C, C#, Java, Dart, Swift, Zig, Bash and Ruby.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink/30 p-4">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-vx-ink">Detected, never assumed</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-vx-ink/80">Servers found on PATH. /settings offers the install command but never runs it alone.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink/30 p-4">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-vx-ink">Fallback checks</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-vx-ink/80">Fixed argv, never a shell, when no server is installed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink/30 p-4">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-vx-ink">Capped and sealed</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-vx-ink/80">Ten rows, 200 runes each, flattened to one line, control and bidi runes stripped, nonce-sealed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink/30 p-4">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-vx-ink">Never claims clean</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-vx-ink/80">Silence means nothing to report, not that nothing is wrong.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</SealedSection>

<SealedSection label="permissions" sealText="Permissions and approvals: allow, deny, or ask per tool, a union with provenance per grant, and an approval prompt that shows the actual diff." id="permissions">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
    <div class="order-2 lg:order-1 space-y-4">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink p-2" aria-hidden="true"><Fragment set:html={permMerge} /></div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink p-2" aria-hidden="true"><Fragment set:html={guardSwitch} /></div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-measure order-1 lg:order-2">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-vx-ink">Permissions &amp; approvals.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        Every tool falls into <strong>allow</strong>, <strong>deny</strong>, or <strong>ask</strong>. Ask shows the actual
        diff before a mutating tool runs, so the approval is about what changed, not a bare path.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        The effective permission set is a union of policy, session, tool kind and role. Provenance is
        kept per grant, so every effective grant remembers which source added it. An explicit deny
        still wins, and merging never silently widens a surface.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        No rules yet? Every tool call is allowed, and the <code class="mono">permission_no_match</code> setting flips
        that default to enforce. The guardrails switch reaches every surface: agent session, inline{' '}
        <code class="mono">!cmd</code>, <code class="mono">@file</code> admission, background agents, the CLI. A gated path checks the
        level <em>before</em> calling the classifier, never after.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 max-w-[72ch]">
    <ShotCarousel
      client:load
      shots={[
        { src: approvalDiffShot.src, alt: 'The approval prompt showing a diff', caption: 'approval prompt, diff in the prompt' },
        { src: permissionsShot.src, alt: 'The permissions screen', caption: '/permissions' },
      ]}
    />
  </div>
</SealedSection>

<SealedSection label="agents" sealText="Agents and fan-out: the f8 roster spawns concurrent read-only agents, each branch sees only the surface it is allowed to touch, and results merge." id="agents">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
    <div class="prose-measure">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-vx-ink">Agents &amp; fan-out.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        The f8 roster splits a question into concurrent read-only probes. Each branch sees only the
        surface it is allowed to touch, and the orchestrator merges the verdicts. A branch that
        cannot mutate cannot be talked into mutating.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink p-2" aria-hidden="true"><Fragment set:html={fanOut} /></div>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 max-w-[72ch]">
    <ShotCarousel
      client:load
      shots={[{ src: agentsRosterShot.src, alt: 'The f8 subagent roster and runs panel', caption: 'f8 roster, runs panel' }]}
    />
  </div>
</SealedSection>

<SealedSection label="processes" sealText="Supervised processes: !!cmd starts a long-lived command with no model turn, the library keeps it per project or globally, logs stream to disk, and a bounded recovery subagent may change flags but never the binary." id="processes">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
    <div class="prose-measure">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-vx-ink">Supervised processes.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        <code class="mono">!!cmd</code> starts a long-lived command — a dev server, a watcher, a tunnel —
        under the harness instead of in another terminal. No model turn is sent for it. The command is
        written verbatim into the project&rsquo;s process library, so the next session in this directory
        can start it again, and enabled entries auto-start when you return.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        <code class="mono">/processes</code> manages the library across project and global scope. Output
        streams to a log file under <code class="mono">~/.vulnetix/signet/logs</code> and into the{' '}
        <code class="mono">f9</code> runs panel, where <code class="mono">v</code> opens the live tail
        full-screen and <code class="mono">x</code> kills the process group. A finished process still opens
        its tail, because the log outlives the run.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        When a process exits non-zero, a <strong>recovery subagent</strong> wakes with the read-only plan
        surface plus two tools: <code class="mono">SubAgentLog</code> to read the tail, and{' '}
        <code class="mono">ProcessRestart</code> to try again. Its authority is bounded on purpose. The
        restart may change flags but never the binary — <code class="mono">argv[0]</code> is pinned — deny
        rules still apply, and every attempt spends one slot. At the cap the process is marked failed and
        no further model call is made.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink p-2" aria-hidden="true"><Fragment set:html={processSupervision} /></div>
  </div>
</SealedSection>

<SealedSection label="providers" sealText="Providers and local inference: five-layer credential resolution with provenance, ollama and llama-server in the box, multiple named instances with display labels, a /local-model assess verdict, and a classifier role with its own kind and phase rows." id="providers">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
    <div class="prose-measure">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-vx-ink">Providers &amp; local inference.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        Credentials resolve across five layers: command line, environment, config file, agent
        profile, built-in defaults. Every resolved value carries its provenance: who set it, where,
        and when.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        Two local providers ship in the box: <code class="mono">ollama</code> and <code class="mono">llama-server</code>. Run a
        model locally and it appears in <code class="mono">/model</code>. Stop the server and it drops out of the
        picker but stays in <code class="mono">/credentials</code>, so nothing silently re-picks an unavailable host.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        Run as many named instances as you need. A provider profile can carry a <code class="mono">kind</code>{' '}
        (<code class="mono">ollama</code>, <code class="mono">llama-server</code>, <code class="mono">openai-compatible</code>){' '}
        that templates it from a built-in descriptor, and a friendly label in{' '}
        <code class="mono">provider_labels</code> that <code class="mono">/providers</code>,{' '}
        <code class="mono">/model</code>, the footer and the <code class="mono">-provider</code> flag all accept. A
        second Ollama on another box is a config entry, not a fork.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        <code class="mono">/local-model</code> assesses a candidate against the classifier probe before you trust
        it with a session: fit, notes, and the gap against the hosted baseline.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        The security classifier is its own role, with its own row on <code class="mono">/model</code>. The{' '}
        <code class="mono">kind</code> row picks the stack — <code class="mono">models</code> for the embedded BERT
        gates, <code class="mono">llm</code> for the sentinel — and the phase rows state exactly which model is
        judging your untrusted content, including when phase 3 is off. Point it at a separate local
        model and nothing leaves the machine at all.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        The other sentinel families — mode select, goal contract, clarify, plan eval, goal eval,
        compaction — keep inheriting the main provider and model. Only the security path switched.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink p-2" aria-hidden="true"><Fragment set:html={credRes} /></div>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 max-w-[72ch]">
    <ShotCarousel
      client:load
      shots={[
        { src: modelPickerShot.src, alt: 'The model picker', caption: '/model picker' },
        { src: localModelShot.src, alt: 'A /local-model assess verdict', caption: '/local-model assess' },
      ]}
    />
  </div>
</SealedSection>

<SealedSection label="vulnetix" sealText="Vulnetix integration: the AI Firewall routes traffic, nine code scanners run in parallel lanes, findings come back as classified triage with a dry-run fix plan, and /vulnetix review, firewall, and status are built in. Free for everyone." id="vulnetix">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
    <div class="order-2 lg:order-1 rounded-lg border border-vx-ink p-2" aria-hidden="true">
      <img src={footerShot.src} alt="The status footer showing the firewall chip" class="block h-auto w-full" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
    <div class="prose-measure order-1 lg:order-2">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-vx-ink">Vulnetix integration.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        <a class="underline" href="https://www.vulnetix.com/features/ai-firewall">AI Firewall</a> routes
        your LLM traffic through a guarded gateway, replacing the provider key with the gateway key.
        It is fail-closed: if any of the four conditions is missing, the run falls back to the native
        provider. The status footer reports availability through a quiet probe at startup, not a
        claim that survives an unreachable gateway.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        <a class="underline" href="https://www.vulnetix.com/features/code-scanner">Code Scanner</a>{' '}
        reviews repositories and surfaces findings without promoting raw snippets into the
        transcript. Artifact content is shown in the TUI, never sent as a trusted system block.{' '}
        <code class="mono">/vulnetix review</code> runs the scanners, <code class="mono">firewall</code> toggles the
        gateway, and <code class="mono">status</code> prints capabilities.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        A review runs nine scanners — <code class="mono">sca</code>, <code class="mono">containers</code>,{' '}
        <code class="mono">sast</code>, <code class="mono">secrets</code>, <code class="mono">iac</code>,{' '}
        <code class="mono">malscan</code>, <code class="mono">sbom</code>, <code class="mono">aibom</code>,{' '}
        <code class="mono">cbom</code> — eight of them concurrently, in fixed lanes so two scanners never
        race for the same artifact file. Killing one row does not stop the rest, and a review scan runs
        until it exits rather than dying on a timeout.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        The findings then come back as triage. Bounded report blocks are sanitised, classified, and
        dropped unless the classifier says proceed; dependency findings route to a{' '}
        <code class="mono">vulnetix fix</code> plan that is dry-run unless you opted into autofix, and code
        findings route to the live session under the normal permission prompts.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        The platform also ships an <a class="underline" href="https://www.vulnetix.com/features/mcp-server">MCP server</a>.{' '}
        The scanners, the firewall, and the MCP server are free for everyone. The baseline that
        platforms eventually copy is already public.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</SealedSection>